        {
          "id": 2237027262,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> So you will need to convert/compact capsa captures before fuzzing them?\n\nSo far it seems libFuzzer is doing a decent job of generating its own corpus for most ~~protocols~~ file formats, _even without being given any seeds at all_.  But yes, if we do want to seed the corpus with actual capsa captures, they will need to go through a trivial conversion to trim out the part that we would now seek past.  I'm keen to start extracting code-coverage data and see where we still have gaps.\n\nI can see the Catapult code you mention (and Guy's comment there)... will need to dig a bit deeper before I understand what it's doing though. :grinning:",
