        {
          "id": 2237199351,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "It might not be at all relevant to you at all, but the aim of that code was to not fuzz the part of the payload that was effectively in-line metadata passed by the wiretap module (to avoid growing the per-frame union), but only to start at genuine payload that would be handed off to other dissectors.  If I understand right, editcap was only changing payload, not the file or packet headers of the file format. As Guy says above, I was thinking of only case 2, whereas you are now planning to tackle case 1.",
